  "index_correspondence": "word[i]=(q_(i+1),mu_(i+1)); word.take k is the chronological k-pair prefix. scale is the finite product. contribution_at identifies mu_(i+1) times scale(word.drop(i+1)); sum folds these contributions with empty sum zero. evaluate_snoc is the manuscript recurrence.",
  "hypotheses": "Polynomial expansion/additive perturbation use explicit commutative-semiring laws and even allow zero multipliers. Difference and guarded ratio use the existing explicit FieldData. The manuscript restricts q_i!=0; NonzeroMultipliers and scale_nonzero capture that restriction. Only the ratio needs y!=x, giving a nonzero actual denominator. No analytic limit or smallness assumption.",
